commands:
mkdir -p reports/offline_de
cd harness && make test

design: receiver uses dedupe::Window with base_seq plus a circular bitmap of W sequence numbers. W defaults to 65536 and is controlled by --dedupe-window. --dedupe-disable restores the old last_seq gate for A/B probes.
arrival_order: accepted frames publish immediately in arrival order. The receiver does not buffer to reorder.
classification: seq below base_seq is too_old, a set bit is duplicate, a sequence beyond base_seq + W slides the window and counts unset retired bits as lost_confirmed.
counters: accepted, duplicates, too_old, lost_confirmed, window_slides, max_reorder_depth are printed on receiver exit.
before_behavior: receiver.cpp previously accepted only hdr->seq_id > last_seq and counted all other packets as duplicates, so any packet reordered behind a later packet was permanently discarded.
after_behavior: adjacent swaps and packets delayed within W are accepted; packets delayed beyond W are too_old.
rejected_alternative: buffering until sequence order was rejected because it adds latency and hides arrival-order behavior.
